From: Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: compile fcconffile.c and build fc-genconf

The Autotools build was never updated for the fc-genconf feature added in
2.18.0: src/fcconffile.c is missing from libfontconfig_la_SOURCES (it is
listed in src/meson.build), and fc-genconf is missing from SUBDIRS even
though configure.ac generates fc-genconf/Makefile.

FcConfigFileGenerate() is declared in the public header
fontconfig/fontconfig.h.in, so on Windows the generated .def file exports
a symbol that no object defines:

    Cannot export FcConfigFileGenerate: symbol not defined

On other platforms the symbol is silently absent from the shared library.

--- a/src/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/Makefile.am
@@ -137,6 +137,7 @@
 	fccache.c \
 	fccfg.c \
 	fccharset.c \
+	fcconffile.c \
 	fccompat.c \
 	fcdbg.c \
 	fcdefault.c \
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #  PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
 
 SUBDIRS=fontconfig fc-case fc-lang fc-const fc-genericfamily src \
-	fc-cache fc-cat fc-conflist fc-list fc-match \
+	fc-cache fc-cat fc-conflist fc-genconf fc-list fc-match \
 	fc-pattern fc-query fc-scan fc-validate conf.d \
 	its po po-conf test
 if ENABLE_DOCS
